WEBVTT

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.450
<i>At last, next month shall be
the post-renovation reopening:</i>

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.780
<i>Puzzle In Resort!</i>

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:20.620
<i>You too can take on
thrilling and exciting</i>

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.050
<i>
puzzle challenges for big prizes.</i>

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:23.470
<i>Get 'em!</i>

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:28.800
<i>I, Genius Okudera, the Puzzle King,</i>

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.210
<i>have overseen production of this hotel.</i>

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.890
<i>I shall introduce you to a
world heretofore unknown!</i>

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:37.660
Kaito, isn't this the
person you saved from some

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.660
underground puzzle ruins last time?

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:41.250
Looks like it.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:45.990
Who's this?

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:47.770
Hello?

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.440
<i>Well, it's been a while!</i>

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:51.540
Um...

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.190
Who are you again?

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.560
<i>You cannot say you've
already forgotten it:</i>

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.560
<i>the beautiful voice of I,
the world-renowned Puzzle King!</i>

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.170
<i>Genius Okudera?!</i>

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:03.620
<i>I wish to share a pleasant time...</i>

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:05.030
<i>with you.</i>

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.760
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:29.490
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.340
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:34.080
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:38.590
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:43.300
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.520
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:48.170
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:50.180
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:52.480
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:54.420
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.240
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.740
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.040
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:08.730
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:10.950
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:13.290
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.920
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:21.810
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:27.490
Brain diver

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:32.290
Brain diver

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:41.010
Crab! Hot Springs! The Puzzle King!

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.510
You're inviting me to the hotel?

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:46.420
<i>Yes! I thought I would
entrust you with the</i>

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:48.460
<i>duty of assistant to the Puzzle King,</i>

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:50.850
<i>to solve the Crown Jewel Puzzle!</i>

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:52.490
Crown Jewel Puzzle?!

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:56.360
<i>It is the featured puzzle of this
to-be-reopened hotel.</i>

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:01.440
<i>Whosoever solves it shall
receive a magnificent prize,</i>

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:03.370
Get a Super Prize!

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.370
thus making it the Crown Jewel Puzzle!

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:06.490
Still, I'm sure none of the guests
will be able to solve it.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:11.750
The reason for which is,
the puzzle is in fact...

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.560
<i>the Puzzle of God!</i>

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:15.500
Don't tell me...

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.550
Hey, wait!

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:19.260
You're making that a selling
point for the hotel?!

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:22.720
Consumers these days want the real thing.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:25.910
That's right, he doesn't know how

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.770
terrifying the Puzzle of God really is.

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:31.490
Fine, I'll solve that puzzle,

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:33.440
so don't let any of the guests near it!

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.020
<i>What's with that tone?!</i>

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.080
<i>I placed eighth in the
Asian preliminaries</i>

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:40.770
<i>of the Puzzle World Cup!</i>

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.740
Don't brag about being
eighth in the prelims.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:45.930
Ana?

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.770
Who is that? Who is calling me?

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.590
<i>Kaito Daimon?</i>

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:04.050
We ran across him while monitoring

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:07.140
that noteworthy pest Genius Okudera.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:07.140
TRANSMITTING

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:08.950
<i>What shall we do?</i>

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.570
A foolish question.

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:14.410
The only thing he is headed for...

00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:15.810
is death.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.960
Let's have him meet a splendid end.

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:28.510
We're here! Hokkaido!

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:30.590
I'm gonna eat a ton!

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:32.840
Um, crab, right?

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:33.960
And sorghum, right?

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:35.440
And crab, right?

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:36.950
And grilled mutton, right?

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:38.180
And crab, right?

00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:39.420
And crab, right?!

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.690
I'm here to solve the puzzle, that's it.

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:43.920
Why are you even here?

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:44.890
Where's the harm?

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:48.040
That Puzzle King said as many of us
could come as we want.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.680
I, Ana, think so too!

00:04:51.110 --> 00:04:52.250
Ana!

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:53.460
It's wide-o!

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:54.690
Hokkaido!

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.980
It's wide-o! Hokkaido!

00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:57.580
-What the hell are you two doing?!

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:58.690
-Hey!

00:04:57.580 --> 00:05:00.050
-It's wide-o! Hokkaido!

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:02.530
Just how long do you intend
to keep me waiting?!

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:02.530
Puzzle King

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:09.200
Put simply, you duped the hotel manager?

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:11.900
Don't speak badly of others!

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:14.830
As Japan's authority on puzzles,

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:17.390
I merely gave the management advice!

00:05:17.390 --> 00:05:18.210
How?

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:21.060
As it turns out, I knew
that the manager's

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.290
deceased's grandfather had made a puzzle.

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:25.280
I suggested he use that,

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:27.490
developing the neighboring area

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:30.560
to create the greatest of puzzle resorts!

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:33.050
To which the manager agreed.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:35.900
While you relieve him
of a boatload of cash,

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:38.070
under the name of an "advisor's fee."

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:41.610
Such rudeness! It is valid compensation!

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:46.090
<i>So, the dead grandpa was a Giver, huh?</i>

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:50.490
Hey, so is it really the Puzzle of God?

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:53.240
You're saying my instincts are mistaken?

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.570
"Instincts"?

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.450
Come on, gimme a break.

00:05:57.450 --> 00:06:01.750
But why make Kaito your
assistant to solve it?

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.420
Management told me,

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:07.130
"We at the hotel would like to
know the solution ahead of time."

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:10.060
But Puzzle King, why not
just solve it yourself?

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:13.740
I though that in the
future, I could bequeath

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:16.040
the title of Puzzle King to Kaito.

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:17.400
But doing so requires a trial,

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:20.560
like a lion throwing its cub into the valley!

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:23.720
What do you think? Quite the honor, yes?

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:27.820
That's one title I don't need...

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:38.600
This whole area is being
turned into a resort.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:41.290
I heard it again.

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:54.400
Welcome to the temple of amusement,
the Puzzle In Resort.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:56.600
I am the manager, Kitao Michiumi.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:01.210
You are the Puzzle King's disciple
Kaito Daimon, correct?

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:03.110
Huh? Disciple?!

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:06.110
I am grateful for your help.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:08.440
I have a dream!

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:12.530
A big dream, for this area
to become one giant resort!

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:16.240
But that will require your skills.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:18.530
This region is being developed into

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:20.530
a resort area at a fever pitch.

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:23.560
If my ideas were to be incorporated,

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:25.900
my dream would be sure to come true.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:30.260
Please! Please, please
lend us your skills!

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:34.110
Everyone, I'm sure you're
tired after your long journey.

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:36.260
Let's have you challenge
the puzzle tomorrow.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:40.770
Come, make yourselves at home.

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:38.270
Get a Super Prize!
Challenge the
Crown Jewel of Puzzles!

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:47.140
Come, order anything you like.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:51.530
The menus are in code.

00:07:51.530 --> 00:07:53.310
What shall you do?!

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:56.230
Let me know when you would like a hint!

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:58.240
Have you decided what you'd like?

00:07:58.480 --> 00:07:59.980
I'll take a coffee.

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.500
I, Ana, will have the "local parfait."

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:03.120
Wh..Wha?!

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:06.150
Huh, this becomes a maze?

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:07.630
Wait, wait!

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:15.890
There's a chapel!

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:19.090
They sure are thorough...

00:08:20.490 --> 00:08:23.990
The Puzzle of God,
in the middle of the wilderness, huh?

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:28.080
What kind of traps will it have?

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.740
Ah, Kaito, you're here!

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.660
Wh..What're you doin', Ana?!

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:39.950
I, Ana, tried seeing how far I could
swim in the outdoor bath.

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:39.950
Whoa, hey! Wait!

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:42.670
Huh? What's wrong, Kaito?

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:44.080
Your cheeks are red.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:46.310
I..I've been in the bath too long!

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:47.550
I know this:

00:08:47.550 --> 00:08:50.030
Ana and Kaito are both boys.

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:51.380
They're both boys...

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:56.110
I, Ana, think you have beautiful skin.

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:55.380
Hey! Hey!

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:58.100
Wh..What?!

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.430
But so do I!

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:00.710
Look!

00:09:00.710 --> 00:09:03.970
Like here, and here, and even here!

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:05.990
St..Stop! I don't need to see that!

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:11.120
What is this?

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:14.620
This coiled, pent-up feeling in my chest?

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:18.080
Oh! It must be crab!

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:21.620
The crab awaiting us on tonight's
dinner table would do that!

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:26.000
The time limit is thirty seconds!

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:28.460
If you can solve it, the
crab is all you can eat.

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:30.940
If you can't, you don't eat.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:32.760
Um, what is this?

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:34.920
And... Begin!

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:39.260
Done.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:40.850
What?!
Me too.

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:44.470
H..Hey, wait!

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:45.740
Order, please.

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:47.130
Very well.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:48.530
Here's horsehair and snow crab.

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:49.350
And king crab!

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:50.440
Very well.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:55.520
Here you are.

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:57.420
Time's up!

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:01.910
This is delicious.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:04.660
My apologies, it's the hotel rule.

00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:09.670
Wait, don't go!

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:12.150
Come back, crab!

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:14.110
Crab, back!

00:10:35.550 --> 00:10:37.460
How cruel.

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:40.700
Can't sleep?

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:47.510
This will soon be reborn,

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:50.830
into a puzzle amusement
park for all to enjoy.

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:53.630
Please visit us again when it's complete.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.720
You'll be my guest.

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:06.970
Yes, I'll try.

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:15.520
Kaito!

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:18.690
Hey, Kaito, Ana's gone!

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:21.030
You're in the same room, right?

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:22.610
Why didn't you notice?

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:23.780
I ain't his guardian!

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:28.120
Your guest left early this
morning to do some painting.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:29.920
I see!

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:31.890
I'll go look for him.

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:34.130
It would be bad if he got lost.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:37.300
Kaito, will you be all right without me?

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:40.130
Who do you think you're talkin' to?

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:42.170
Okay, I'll be back!

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:46.140
Kaito Daimon shall soon
attempt the puzzle.

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:49.590
TRANSMITTING

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:48.520
<i>Your orders?</i>

00:11:50.440 --> 00:11:53.670
Kaito Daimon, this is your...

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:56.720
final puzzle!

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:00.100
This big-ass garden is?

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:02.390
Yes, the Crown Jewel of Puzzles.

00:12:02.390 --> 00:12:05.550
To release the sealed prize,

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:05.430
Bamboo Fountain                   Rock
Garden                     Door to the Prize

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:09.100
Torch
Bamboo Fountain                   Rock Garden                     Door to the Prize

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:09.120
one must solve three puzzles
and obtain the password.

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:11.750
Incidentally, there are rules for

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:13.360
the routes constituting this puzzle,

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:14.630
so please be careful.

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:15.840
Rules?

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:18.790
Yes, you may solve the puzzles
in any order you like,

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:22.770
but you must take all
paths at least once.

00:12:22.770 --> 00:12:24.590
Like a one-stroke sketch, huh?

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:30.020
Protégé, what are you doing?!

00:12:35.180 --> 00:12:36.750
Is something the matter?

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:38.400
Could it be you've lost your nerve?

00:12:38.740 --> 00:12:39.950
Yeah, right.

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:41.650
Don't get in my way this time.

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:45.630
Whatever are you saying, young Kaito?

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:47.170
You, my assistant, can handle something

00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:49.110
like this on your own, yes?

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:53.000
Well, let's get started.

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:55.620
Puzzle time, let's begin!

00:12:57.250 --> 00:12:59.600
I said I'd look for him,

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:02.160
but how should I look, and where?

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:10.160
Over there, maybe!

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:14.990
First up are the Bedazzling Torches.

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:18.490
So, you have to light
'em in the proper order.

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:20.800
A difficult task from the start.

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:23.690
Look at the signboards lined
up next to the torches.

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:32.110
There are some numerals
in circles and some not.

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:34.580
What could that signify?

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:35.830
Solved it.

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:37.080
What?!

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:39.070
The un-circled numbers are

00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:41.650
the number of consecutive ones to light.

00:13:41.650 --> 00:13:42.800
The circled numbers are

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.700
the number of non-consecutive
ones to light.

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:47.050
In other words...

00:13:53.540 --> 00:13:55.810
The password is "KA" if
written phonetically.

00:13:56.210 --> 00:13:58.330
Or the Chinese character
meaning "strength."

00:13:58.330 --> 00:14:01.340
You are indeed my protégé!

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:05.780
It looks like there was no trap set here.

00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:06.900
But...

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:09.200
Just what is this puzzle?

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:11.370
Is it really...

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:15.910
I knew you'd be here!

00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:22.420
Ana, couldn't you have said
something before you went out?

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.570
Ana!

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:27.680
Hey, are you listening?

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:44.110
Solved it!

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:46.740
The answer to this puzzle is "six"!

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:49.140
Such fearsome speed!

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:52.100
I mean, well done, my protégé!

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:54.060
This puzzle too...

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:03.170
I wonder if Kaito's okay.

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:07.230
Well, I guess him being him,
there's no need to worry.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:23.160
This area will become
an amusement park, huh?

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:27.550
Still, I feel kind of sad...

00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:30.360
That person feels the same.

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:33.170
You talked to someone?

00:15:40.050 --> 00:15:43.050
You're finished? How'd it go?

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:44.860
What's this?

00:15:51.390 --> 00:15:52.930
Ana!

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:58.560
The answer to this is...

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:03.480
I

00:15:59.010 --> 00:16:00.010
"I"!

00:16:00.010 --> 00:16:03.480
That's the way that leads to the
entrance of the stone torch up ahead.

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:06.030
Well, a decent job, I'd say.

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:08.810
This means you've gathered
two of the passwords

00:16:08.810 --> 00:16:11.530
to open the door leading
to the sealed prize, eh?

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:14.280
There was no trap in this puzzle either.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:16.070
On the contrary...

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:17.740
That's it!

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:25.880
Are you okay, Ana?

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:35.140
Th..This isn't the Puzzle of God?!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.680
What does that mean?

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:40.060
These feel warm, like...

00:16:40.860 --> 00:16:44.050
They're fun, these puzzles
your grandpa made.

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:48.110
If they were deadly, they
wouldn't feel this way.

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:51.440
So, the only thing to do is have fun!

00:16:57.450 --> 00:17:01.170
We have to take all the
paths in this garden,

00:17:01.170 --> 00:17:03.420
like a one-stroke sketch.

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:04.760
Right?

00:17:04.760 --> 00:17:06.000
Yes, that's right.

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:09.870
But there's something I thought was
strange when I saw the map:

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:11.660
If that's the goal,

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:14.010
there's no way to do it
like a one-stroke sketch.

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:16.010
You knew that in just an instant?!

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:19.820
But if the rock garden were the goal,

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:22.110
then the sketch could be completed.

00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:26.040
Meaning, there must be a
route leading to that door.

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:28.110
There is no such route.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:31.850
Look! No route is on the map!

00:17:31.850 --> 00:17:33.030
This, huh?

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:35.530
What are you doing?

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:39.080
I get it.

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:51.000
A bridge was hidden among the bamboo!

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:54.670
If we cross this and enter
the three passwords...

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:01.100
For him to solve them this quickly...

00:18:02.070 --> 00:18:04.770
But the game ends here.

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:20.530
Look out!

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:24.120
Impossible!

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:26.470
Thank you for bringing us here.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.920
The first password is "I."

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:39.180
Next is "6," phonetically, "MU".

00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:41.100
And the order of those lamps...

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:44.850
That was written as "KA".

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:47.810
IMUKA? What's that mean?

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:49.070
It's backwards.

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:50.870
It should be KAMUI.

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:53.490
In the Ainu language, it means "god."

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:56.490
Ah, that's right, I've
just remembered as much!

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:59.780
A prize sealed up by the god of Hokkaido?

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:01.070
How romantic!

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:03.330
This is the last one.

00:19:07.030 --> 00:19:07.920
All right!

00:19:07.920 --> 00:19:08.910
We've done it!

00:19:09.190 --> 00:19:11.020
What do you think will come out?

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:12.250
I can't wait!

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:14.780
That person has prepared the

00:19:14.780 --> 00:19:16.750
greatest of prizes beyond the door,

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:20.740
to soothe the dried hearts
of those who visit.

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:32.520
This is a prize?

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:40.010
"The voices of the trees."

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:41.820
"The murmur of the water."

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:43.980
"The voices of the birds and animals."

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:45.970
"They are treasures."

00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:47.380
"Treasures that belong to us all."

00:19:48.190 --> 00:19:50.040
How do you know those words?

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:00.010
That scene!

00:20:08.830 --> 00:20:13.830
My grandfather often brought me here
when I was young.

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:15.690
It's a place of memories.

00:20:20.510 --> 00:20:24.200
Convey that to others,
what lay in your grandfather's heart.

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:28.660
I may have forgotten something important.

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:33.690
Now then, we've solved
your grandfather's puzzle,

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:37.420
so development on the resort
can continue in earnest!

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:41.410
I'm very sorry, Mr. Genius,

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:45.880
but the aim of this
hotel has just shifted.

00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:48.660
As such, your advisor's fee shall only

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:50.970
be paid till the end of this month.

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:53.270
For real?!

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:58.450
It seems that Kaito Daimon's
companions interfered.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:02.070
Why couldn't we stop them?

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:07.810
Unbelievable, the lot of you.

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:09.660
Are none of you of use?!

00:21:10.610 --> 00:21:12.910
"Companions," indeed!

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:27.000
It looks like the manager's grandpa
used to be a POG Giver.

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:30.800
Then he retired, and made that
bed-and-breakfast's garden puzzle.

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:34.530
I'm sure that, once free
of the POG's leash,

00:21:34.530 --> 00:21:37.390
he tried with all his heart to make people
have fun with his puzzles.

00:21:37.390 --> 00:21:40.760
I felt that clearly through his puzzles.

00:21:40.760 --> 00:21:42.230
Oh, really?

00:21:51.820 --> 00:21:53.840
Say, Ana.

00:21:55.700 --> 00:21:57.600
Was it true when you
said you could hear the

00:21:57.600 --> 00:21:59.630
voice of the manager's grandfather?

00:22:02.100 --> 00:22:03.310
I knew it!

00:22:03.310 --> 00:22:05.720
No matter how odd you are, there's no way

00:22:05.720 --> 00:22:08.330
you could talk to ghosts, right?

00:22:08.330 --> 00:22:10.510
Hey, hurry up already.

00:22:10.510 --> 00:22:12.010
The plane will leave!

00:22:12.010 --> 00:22:14.020
Oh, no! Let's hurry, Ana!

00:22:37.270 --> 00:22:41.490
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.490 --> 00:22:47.410
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.410 --> 00:22:52.040
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:57.090
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.250 --> 00:23:02.570
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.570 --> 00:23:07.930
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.800 --> 00:23:13.110
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.110 --> 00:23:18.360
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.360 --> 00:23:23.700
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:23.700 --> 00:23:26.380
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:29.290
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.290 --> 00:23:33.860
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.860 --> 00:23:39.160
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.160 --> 00:23:44.440
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.440 --> 00:23:49.980
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:49.980 --> 00:23:58.920
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:02.250 --> 00:24:04.630
Are preparations for the
Gakuen's festival going well?

00:24:04.630 --> 00:24:06.830
Yes, everything is according to plan.

00:24:06.830 --> 00:24:08.420
I see...

00:24:08.420 --> 00:24:11.660
Having a gifted student council president
is something of a dilemma.

00:24:11.660 --> 00:24:13.080
Meaning what?

00:24:13.080 --> 00:24:16.750
If everything is going well,
there is no need for me to appear.

00:24:16.750 --> 00:24:20.730
I'll just watch the setting sun
from the principal's office...

00:24:20.730 --> 00:24:24.440
Next time:
"The Fallen Apple & the Path's Continuation"

00:24:24.440 --> 00:24:27.410
Mr. Principal, please do your job.
